format: 2
name: an escape in a string literal is decoded as Java decodes it (T22, fixed)
class: Probe
method: m
arg: 01
expect: AGREE
note: Found by the trace-payload case (ADR-063 r4). PirGenerator lowered a StringLiteralExpr with
note: getValue(), JavaParser's source text with its escapes, so the script held a backslash and an n
note: where Java holds a line break.
note: Fixed by #256: string literals are decoded as javac decodes them, so both sides trace a line
note: break. Before the fix the expectation was DIVERGE T22, with UPLC tracing "a\\n[TRACE] b".
---
import org.julclang.core.PlutusData;
import org.julclang.stdlib.Builtins;

public class Probe {
    public static PlutusData m(PlutusData n) {
        return Builtins.trace("a\n[TRACE] b", n);
    }
}
